      "content": "{\n \"_about\": \"Recorded and constructed reasoning outputs for #804/#1058. 25 entries from PR #525's corpus (talisp, 47Hunter47 and reviewers) and 12 live strandings recovered by 47Hunter47 (https://gist.github.com/47Hunter47/4abcd3a80701f5634f85b96e4c067cc3). 'calls' = the tool names delivered as calls under the #1058 rules. Mixed tails (a declared call beside a wrapper call naming no declared tool): the declared call is delivered, the wrapper stays reasoning.\",\n \"specimens\": [\n  {\n   \"name\": \"act-natural-stop\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The user asked what the file contains. Reading it first is the right step, and then I can summarize what is inside.\\n\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\",\n   \"calls\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"act-first-text\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\",\n   \"calls\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"act-two-adjacent\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The comparison needs both files. I will read them one after the other.\\n\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\",\n   \"calls\": [\n    \"execute_code\",\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"envelope-undeclared\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The tool for this step is not in my visible list, so it goes through the wrapper with a single entry.\\n\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=tool_call>\\n<parameter=calls>\\n[{\\\"name\\\": \\\"execute_code\\\", \\\"arguments\\\": {\\\"code\\\": \\\"print(1)\\\"}}]\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"envelope-declared\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\",\n    \"tool_call\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The tool for this step is not in my visible list, so it goes through the wrapper with a single entry.\\n\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=tool_call>\\n<parameter=calls>\\n[{\\\"name\\\": \\\"execute_code\\\", \\\"arguments\\\": {\\\"code\\\": \\\"print(1)\\\"}}]\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\",\n   \"calls\": [\n    \"tool_call\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-backticks-midsentence\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Before answering, a note on the wire protocol: I must emit `<tool_call>` then `<function=execute_code>` - the format.\\nWith that settled, the plan is clear.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-midsentence-whole-call\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The format is <tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call> ok.\\nI will follow it for the real call next.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-backticks-line-start\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Plan:\\n`<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>` comes next.\\nThat is the shape the harness wants.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-line-start-no-function\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Next step:\\n<tool_call> is the tag the format starts with.\\nThe parameters follow it.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-line-start-other-tag\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Example:\\n<tool_call>\\n<parameter=code>\\nx\\n</parameter>\\nThe body would continue here.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-indented\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"As a list:\\n  <tool_call>\\n  <function=execute_code>\\n  ...and so on for each field.\\nThat covers the layout.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-markdown-quote\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"The doc says:\\n> <tool_call>\\n> <function=execute_code>\\nand that is all it says about calling.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-backtick-block\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Format:\\n```xml\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\\n```\\nThat is how a call looks, for reference.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-tilde-block\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"Format:\\n~~~\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\\n~~~\\nDone, that is the whole example.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-tag-before-think-end\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"So I call it:\\n<tool_call>\\n</think>Here is the answer to your question.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\": \"mention-closed-span-fenced\",\n   \"finish\": \"stop\",\n   \"tools\": [\n    \"execute_code\"\n   ],\n   \"input\": \"This is a documentation example, not an action:\\n```xml\\n<tool_call>\\n<function=execute_code>\\n<parameter=code>\\nprint(1)\\n</parameter>\\n</function>\\n</tool_call>\\n```\\nI should explain it without calling any tool.\\n</think>Here is the explanation.\",\n   \"calls\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"name\":